WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.668
-Our next guest is
a Grammy-nominated singer

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.638
and singer/songwriter whose
new show, "Conjuring Kesha,"

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.508
premieres Friday, July 8th
on Discovery+.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.776
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.512
-Energy, spirit, ghost, demon,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.548
whatever is in here,
how's it going?

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.585
I'm gonna do
a ghost-box session.

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:23.523
Hopefully I can talk to a nice
spirit through this thing.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.291
You can talk into here.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:31.297
You can use this
to tell me your name.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.467
-Please welcome to the show
Kesha, everybody!

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.235
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:44.043 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:51.884 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.220
Welcome to the show, Kesha.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.490
-Thank you.
-I am so excited.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.294
One of my favorite thing about
paranormal investigation shows

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.728
is the tiny flashlight.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.564
And I'm so glad you have --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.799
-Mine's bedazzled.
-Yeah, I could tell.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.335
-Did you notice?
-It's both a tiny flashlight

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.472
that I've grown accustomed to
from these paranormal shows.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.108
And with a real Kesha twist
on it, which is it's bedazzled.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.076
-It sparkled.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.311
-You had a podcast
about the paranormal.

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.714
-I did.
Well, this story goes way back.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.417
And again, I told him this
earlier, I haven't been on

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.486
"Late Night" in like years.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.121
-So we might ramble.
-Okay.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.524
-So if we do, we get her
and we bring her back.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.758
-Okay, gotcha.
-Okay.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.694
-Before I ask about your show,
because you know,

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.263
it is Pride Month and you --
-Oh [bleep] -- Yeah.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.998
Can I --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.166
-What do you mean, "Can I?"

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.934
If you can't, what are you
going to do?

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.469
[ Laughter ]
-Whoops.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.538
-It's totally fine.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.206
You performed at the legendary
Stonewall Inn.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:48.875
-Yes.
-For Pride. Look at that.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:52.511
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.481
I want to ask you, you and your
dancers wore something,

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.316
and guess what the network said.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:02:00.220
"We have to blur it out."

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.221
-I mean, that is making it
seem way worse.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.357
-I agree. I saw this photo
earlier, and it was not --

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:07.760
It did not deserve to be
blurred, but everybody decided.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.161
-That's just beautiful butts.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.496
-Yeah, it was beautiful butts.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.031
-For Pride.
-It was for Pride.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.434
I'm assuming that your dancers
were enthusiastic about

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.835
showing off their beautiful
butts as well.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.903
-Absolutely. Oh, we were in
dance rehearsal, and I was like,

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.606
"Listen, my butthole
is going to be out."

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:23.609
-Okay.
-"So, if you would like to

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:27.112
and feel comfortable,
I invite you to join me."

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:28.514
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:31.184
I will say, I always feel like,
when I'm seeing a show,

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.853
I either want to see
no buttholes or everybody's.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.889
-All the buttholes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:38.791
-Yeah.
-Options!

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.393
-Yeah. I just don't --
'Cause if there's just one,

00:02:41.393 --> 00:02:43.329
then the whole show,
I'm just following that around.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.897
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:48.101
That would be very narcissistic
of me to just be like,

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.436
"Only my butthole."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.438
-Now on to the paranormal, so --

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:56.175
-[ Laughs ]
Speaking of buttholes.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:57.877
-Do ghosts have them?

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.813
-Listen, I --

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.849
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.685
-No, like, when you become a
ghost, do you keep the butthole?

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.321
-I can confirm -- You know what?

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.423
Actually, I might have to go
back on that.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.224
So I have, like, a whole thing.
-Okay.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.026
-I have a thing.
Can I tell you the thing?

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.194
-Great.
-Okay.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.730
So I always loved
the paranormal.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.998
I've had weird experiences.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.067
My whole life has been
very weird.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:24.737
And then during COVID,
I was, like, having, like,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:28.007
existential crisis
after existential crisis

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.377
and just lots of anxiety,
and one night I'm sitting in bed

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:35.781
and I was like,
"Uh-oh.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:37.517
Here we go." And --

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.318
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.954
And I was like,
"My -- My brain's breaking.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.623
I feel it breaking. It's going.
This is me.

00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:47.193
I knew it was going to happen,
but here it goes.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.228
We're going crazy."
-Okay.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:53.899
-And then, like, I heard
a voice, I saw a vision.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.502
My cats brought me headphones.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.270
It's a whole thing.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.174
And, like, I understood what
love was.

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:04.076
I saw the whole universe.

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:06.913
I pulled back.
It was a microcosm of itself.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.282
I got the -- got the picture,
right?

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.483
-Yeah. Sure.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.786
-So the next morning,
I called my therapist

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.722
and I was like,
"Girl, it happened."

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.489
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:18.691
-Did your therapist say,

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.426
"Did the cats bring you
the headphones?"

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.195
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:24.597
-And I was like, "Yep."

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:27.466
And she was like, "Guess what.
Congratulations."

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:28.701
And I was like, "What are you
talking about?"

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.604
She's like,
"This is a spiritual awakening."

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.240
And I was like, "Wait, what?"

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.044
[ Laughter ]
And she was like this, "Yay!"

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.312
And I was like,
"This is the point?

00:04:40.312 --> 00:04:42.514
Like, this is what I've been
working towards?

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:45.251
What? This is terrifying."

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:47.352
And she was like,
"Yeah, welcome."

00:04:47.352 --> 00:04:50.356
And I was like, "Okay."
And so I decided to really,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.626
like, lean into it. I started
writing music about it.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.828
And I called my brother.
That was my next phone call.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:59.031
And I was like, "Okay, my brain
broke. We're leaning into it.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.301
We're making a TV show
about this

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.002
and we're going to go
find some ghosts.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.337
Let's look for some aliens
and [bleep] it.

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:06.906
Let's get Bigfoot."

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:12.010
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.814
-I mean...

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.416
I'll tell you this.
If I was a network executive

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:18.751
and that was your pitch,
I'd be like,

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.653
"We want to do 50 seasons."

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.820
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.456
-Honey, that's the goal.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:26.592
-Now, you have guests.
-Yes.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:29.428
-You travel to sort of places
that you think might be

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.831
inhabited by the spirits,
the paranormal.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.400
Are your guests -- These are
sometimes people you know.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.235
Are they enthusiastic about
taking this journey with you?

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.737
-Yeah, so each episode is
a journey

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.973
to its own special place.
-Okay.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.775
-So I call up my friends

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.744
and the really good ones
are like, "Fine."

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:48.314
And so, like, the first episode

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.616
is Whitney Cummings
is coming with me.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.084
-She's great.
-The best.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:53.252
Such a good friend.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.955
I took her to a haunted prison
in the middle of

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.489
the Tennessee mountains,

00:05:57.489 --> 00:06:01.194
and there was a demon.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.461
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:05.198
There was a demonologist.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:09.435
She's upstairs, like, having
this beautiful moment crying.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:14.373
She believes that she's
connected and is having

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:17.043
a full conversation
with a trans ghost.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.877
-Okay.
-Which may be true.

00:06:18.877 --> 00:06:21.881
-Sure.
-Downstairs, the demonologist is

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.783
screaming,
"Get her out of there!

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.217
It's a demon! It's a trick!"

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:27.452
And I'm sitting there
being like,

00:06:27.452 --> 00:06:31.223
"Um...I'm not going up there
in case it is a demon."

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:33.926
[ Laughter ]
"But, like, Whitney's crying

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.194
and having, like, a really
beautiful, like, experience."

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:38.030
-Yeah. By the way --
-And I'm the host.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:42.668
-Yeah. And as of two minutes
ago, a friend.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.237
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.506
-You literally were like,
"Whitney is the best.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.074
Anyway, I took her to a prison.

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:51.310
She met a demon
and I was like, 'Bye!'"

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:56.816
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.517
I'm very excited
that you have this show.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:00.453
This makes me very happy.
-Listen, it's like --

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.854
If nothing,
it's very entertaining.

00:07:02.854 --> 00:07:05.991
-Yeah. I mean, I also might want
your therapist's number

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:08.127
because I feel like this is
the one I want, where I'm like,

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:11.130
"I lost my mind,"
and she's like, "Monetize it!"

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.533
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.868
This has been an absolute
delight having you here.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.370
Congratulations on your show.
-Thank you.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.805
-Please come back again.
-Oh, I'm coming back.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:21.807
-I feel like you barely --
I mean, if you haven't done

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:24.143
"Late Night" in a long time,
I feel like, you know,

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:26.245
the break paid off.
-Did I do good?

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.313
-You were fantastic.
-Did I do okay, you guys?

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.680
-Give it up for Kesha,
everybody.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.217
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wonderful!

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:35.153
"Conjuring Kesha" premieres
Friday, July 8th on Discovery+.

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.223
We'll be right back
with Patrick Radden Keefe.

